abstract: >-
  ART is a falsifiable theoretical framework for investigating which structures become non-removable when autonomous actors cause consequential changes across trust boundaries. The current research program focuses on Target, Bounded Authority, Verification, and the conditional emergence of Judgment, Delegation, Termination, attribution, responsibility, and settlement.
